//   precondition; otherwise we remain outside, so the implication is vacuous.
//   In the complete-prefix branch, CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut
//   to false, again making the implication vacuous. In the inside-span argmax
//   branch we call AppendConstrainedToken only after IsTokenValidNext returned
//   true, so validity is preserved; in the fallback branch ConstrainedStep
//   supplies a valid next token (or EOS, which breaks), so AppendConstrainedToken
//   also preserves validity.
// suffix: Outside a span, appending a normal token leaves the implication
//   vacuous; opening a span sets currentConstrainedOut := [], and the length-0
//   suffix of generated matches []. CloseConstrainedSpan appends ">>" and resets
//   currentConstrainedOut to [], so the implication is vacuous afterward. Both
//   inside-span append branches use AppendConstrainedToken, which appends the
//   same token to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving the suffix
//   equality.
